        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0488" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg402"/>

                <head>No. 176.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1"
                            type="from">Fish</persName> to General <persName type="to"
                            >Schenck</persName>.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-08-12"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 12,
                        1873</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 427.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 440, of the 5th ultimo,
                    has been received. The Department has been surprised at the statement of Lord
                    Granville, to which it refers, that the communication by <persName
                        corresp="#p_SET1">Sir Edward Thornton</persName> of a copy of his
                    instructions upon the subject of the joint note to the maritime Powers, provided
                    for by the Treaty of Washington, should be regarded as a reply to my note to Sir
                    Edward on that subject. With due deference to the larger experience of Her
                    Majesty’s foreign office on such subjects, it had here been supposed that a
                    reply to a note, to entitle it to be regarded as official or binding on the
                    party which makes it, should be in the same form as the note to which it may
                    purport to be an answer.</p>
                <p>Awaiting a reply of that character, the subject has remained in suspense.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName corresp="#p_HF1">Hamilton Fish</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
